steps.description:
Create a HIGH_SIGNAL_EVENTS constant map that defines the 11 high-signal event types and their payload field names for extraction. This serves as both the filter set and the documentation of what fields each event type provides:

- decision_recorded: { question, selected_option, reasoning, alternatives }
- checkpoint_created: { checkpoint_id, description, state_snapshot }
- retrospective_recorded: { summary, approach, decisions[], challenges[], learnings[], suggestions[], confidence }
- agent_spawned: { agent_name, task_description, agent_role }
- task_completed: { task_id, outcome, duration_ms, result_summary }
- task_failed: { task_id, error, duration_ms, failure_reason, recovery_attempted }
- gate_reached: { gate_id, gate_type, description }
- gate_approved: { gate_id, gate_type, approver, reason }
- gate_rejected: { gate_id, gate_type, approver, reason, required_changes }
- budget_warning: { budget_type, current_usage, threshold, recommendation }
- recovery_strategy_selected: { strategy_name, alternatives_considered[], reasoning, context }

Export this map so tests and documentation can reference it.
